/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/deployments","created_at":"2010-08-24T01:37:33Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T12:20:35Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-11T02:22:05Z","git_url":"git://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:pandas-dev/pandas.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas","homepage":"https://pandas.pydata.org","size":378810,"stargazers_count":47298,"watchers_count":47298,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":19393,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3594,"license":{"key":"bsd-3-clause","name":"BSD 3-Clause \"New\" or \"Revised\" License","spdx_id":"BSD-3-Clause","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/bsd-3-clause","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTU="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["alignment","data-analysis","data-science","flexible","pandas","python"],"visibility":"public","forks":19393,"open_issues":3594,"watchers":47298,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"## description \r\nAs I have to cope with financial data, like an accountant, pivot table is a powerful tool for me.Yet recently, calling method `pandas.DataFrame.pivot_table`, I encountered a problem.\r\nWith data of `General Ledgers` (17 columns and over 7000 rows) I had expected to get a pivot table with values = `debit amount minus credit amount` for each `journal ID`, which identifies each `journal entry`, columns = `account name`, and index = `journal ID`. According to the `primary accounting equation`, for each `journal entry` we have `sum of debit amount` equal `sum of credit amount`. Thus, sum of all data of a big pivot table, whose index is `journal ID`, whose columns is `account name` and whose values are `debit minus credit`, must be zero.\r\nHowever, when having called `pandas.DataFrame.pivot_table`, I found that sum of all data of that pivot table, did not equals zero. To be carefully, I generated a pivot table with `Microsoft Excel`, and it was no doubt that sum of whole pivot table equaled zero.\r\n## code\r\nTalk is cheap, here is the code.\r\n```python\r\n#!/usr/bin/env python\r\nfrom pandas import read_excel\r\nd=read_excel(excel_file_of_gl,sheet_name='Sheet1',header=0,engine='openpyxl')\r\nd.pivot_table(values=['drcr'],index=['jid'],columns=['accna']).to_excel(./data.xlsx')\r\n# 'drcr' means 'debit minus credit','jid' means 'journal id', and 'accna' means 'account name'.\r\n# open the output file, sum of all the 'drcr' value did not equaled zero, which was weird.\r\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/42629/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/42629/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]